ine","attrs":{"latex":"30 \\le t < 40"}},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"(f = 8)"}},{"type":"text","text":". Which interval contains the median?"}]}]},"e":"Cumulative frequencies are 6, 17, 32, 40. For N = 40 the median is at position 20.5, which falls in the class with cumulative frequency 17 to 32: 20 ≤ t < 30.","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Grouped data","st":"median class","cfg":{"question_number":6,"paper_question_key":6,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"A","criterion_label":"Criterion A — Knowing and understanding","criterion_title":"Knowing and understanding","difficulty_level":"basic","marks":1,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","source":"myp4-term1-summative-first-term-2026-version-d"}},{"n":7,"t":"single_choice","p":"From the box-and-whisker diagram below, what is the interquartile range (IQR)?\n\n[Figure: Box-and-whisker diagram]","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"From the box-and-whisker diagram below, what is the interquartile range (IQR)?"}]},{"type":"assessDiagramBlock","attrs":{"spec":{"kind":"box_plot","title":"Box-and-whisker diagram","xLabel":"","xMin":10,"xMax":50,"fiveNumber":{"min":15,"q1":22,"median":30,"q3":40,"max":48},"version":1}}}]},"e":"The box runs from Q1 = 22 to Q3 = 40, so IQR = 40 − 22 = 18.","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Box-and-whisker diagrams","st":"interquartile range","cfg":{"question_number":7,"paper_question_key":7,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"C","criterion_label":"Criterion C — Communicating","criterion_title":"Communicating","difficulty_level":"basic","marks":1,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","source":"myp4-term1-summative-first-term-2026-version-d"}},{"n":8,"t":"single_choice","p":"Five test scores are 68, 70, 72, 74, 76. Including a late sitting outlier of 8 gives six scores. How do the mean and median change?","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Five test scores are 68, 70, 72, 74, 76. Including a late sitting outlier of 8 gives six scores. How do the mean and median change?"}]}]},"e":"Original mean and median are both 72. With 8, the mean is 368/6 ≈ 61.33 (a large fall), while the median is (70 + 72)/2 = 71 (a small fall).","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Effect of outliers","st":"mean and median under an outlier","cfg":{"question_number":8,"paper_question_key":8,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"D","criterion_label":"Criterion D — Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","criterion_title":"Applying mathematics in real-life contexts","difficulty_level":"basic","marks":1,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","source":"myp4-term1-summative-first-term-2026-version-d"}},{"n":9,"t":"single_choice","p":"A population of $N = 4$ values $\\{3, 5, 7, 9\\}$ has mean $\\mu = 6$. What is its population standard deviation $\\sigma$?","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A population of "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"N = 4"}},{"type":"text","text":" values "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\{3, 5, 7, 9\\}"}},{"type":"text","text":" has mean "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\mu = 6"}},{"type":"text","text":". What is its population standard deviation "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\sigma"}},{"type":"text","text":"?"}]}]},"e":"$\\sigma^2=\\frac{9+1+1+9}{4}=5$, so $\\sigma=\\sqrt{5}$.","m":1,"df":"easy","tp":"Population standard deviation","st":"population standard deviation","cfg":{"question_number":9,"paper_question_key":9,"paper_section":"A","myp_criterion":"A","criterion_label":"Criterion A — Knowing and understanding","criterion_title":"Knowing and understanding","difficulty_level":"basic","marks":1,"calculator":true,"calculator_policy":"permitted","assessment_style":"myp_summative","source":"myp4-term1-summative-first-term-2026-versi